QUERY 5: How can LSTM networks model long documents for text classification?
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  ── BM25 Result ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  Title   : Multi-Timescale Long Short-Term Memory Neural Network for Modelling Sentences and Documents
  Abstract:
    Neural network based methods have obtained great progress on a variety of
    natural language processing tasks. However, it is still a challenge task
    to model long texts, such as sentences and documents. In this paper, we
    propose a multi-timescale long short-termmemory (MT-LSTM) neural network
    to model long texts. MTLSTM partitions the hidden states of the standard
    LSTM into several groups. Each group is activated at different time
    periods. Thus, MT-LSTM can model very long documents as well as short
    sentences. Experiments on four benchmark datasets show that our model
    outperforms the other neural models in text classification task.

  [ Annotator 1 relevance: ___1 ]   [ Annotator 2 relevance: ___1 ]

